<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>There is, like Anak’s sons of old,</l><l>A race of giants still:</l><l>Self-glorying, self-confidence,</l><l>Self-seeking and self-will.</l><l>Still must these haughty Anakims</l><l>By Caleb’s sword be slain,</l><l>Ere Hebron’s heights of heav’nly love,</l><l>Our conqu’ring feet can gain.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Oh, save me from self-will, dear Lord,</l><l>Which claims Thy sacred throne;</l><l>Oh! let my will be lost in Thine,</l><l>And let Thy will be done.</l><l>Oh, keep me from self-confidence,</l><l>And self-sufficiency;</l><l>Let me exchange my strength for Thine,</l><l>And lean alone on Thee.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Oh, save me from self-seeking, Lord,</l><l>Let me not be my own;</l><l>A living sacrifice I come,</l><l>Lord, keep me Thine alone.</l><l>From proud vain glory save me, Lord,</l><l>From pride of praise and fame;</l><l>To Christ be all the honor given,</l><l>The glory to His name.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Oh, Savior. slay the self in me</l><l>By Thy consuming breath;</l><l>Show me Thy heart, Thy wounds, Thy shame,</l><l>That self be put to death.</l><l>When the Shekinah flame came down,</l><l>E’en Moses could not stay;</l><l>So let Thy glory fill me now,</l><l>And self forever slay.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
